{% comment %}
  Clippar product page. Two-column on desktop — media left, buy panel right —
  using the same tokens as the landing page so it reads as one site.

  The variant picker is hidden when the product has only a default variant,
  which is the case for the single boxed kit; it appears automatically if
  variants are added later.

  https://shopify.dev/docs/storefronts/themes/architecture/templates/product
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign current_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}

<div class="pdp full-width">
  <div class="pdp-grid">
    <div class="pdp-media">
      {%- if product.media.size > 0 -%}
        {%- for media in product.media -%}
          <div class="pdp-media-item">
            {%- if media.media_type == 'image' -%}
              <img
                src="{{ media | image_url: width: 1400 }}"
                alt="{{ media.alt | escape }}"
                width="{{ media.width }}"
                height="{{ media.height }}"
                loading="{% if forloop.first %}eager{% else %}lazy{% endif %}"
                sizes="(min-width: 900px) 50vw, 100vw"
                srcset="
                  {{ media | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w,
                  {{ media | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w,
                  {{ media | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w
                "
              >
            {%- elsif media.media_type == 'video' -%}
              {{ media | video_tag: image_size: '1400x', controls: true, muted: true, loop: true }}
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="pdp-media-empty">
          <span>No product images yet</span>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="pdp-panel">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="pdp-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h1 class="pdp-title">{{ product.title }}</h1>

      <div class="pdp-price">
        {{ current_variant.price | money }}
        {%- comment -%}
          The strike-through is deliberately behind a setting that defaults to
          OFF, and it is not an aesthetic preference.

          A "was $109, now $99" is a representation that the kit was genuinely
          offered at $109 for a reasonable period beforehand. It never has been
          — it has never been sold at any price. Showing it on day one would be
          a false saving under ACL s18 / s29(1)(i), which is a pattern the ACCC
          has actively pursued. Henry settled this on 24 Aug: $99, shown alone.

          Turn this on only once $109 has actually been the selling price for a
          real period. See decisions/2026-08-24-take-preorders-on-the-kit.md.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.show_compare_at and current_variant.compare_at_price > current_variant.price -%}
          <s class="pdp-compare">{{ current_variant.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Pre-order disclosure.

        This sits above the fold, as rendered text, outside any accordion, and
        that placement is load-bearing three times over:

        - Google Merchant Center requires the expected shipping date to be
          visible on the landing page for anything marked `preorder`, or the
          listing is disapproved.
        - The ACCC requires clear information about "the likely timing of
          production and delivery" before taking payment.
        - It is the single biggest objection a buyer has when handing over $99
          for a thing that does not exist yet.

        The cancel-any-time promise is what makes a soft month honest. Suppliers
        have quoted nothing, so the date is a forecast; rather than dress it up,
        we say so and carry the risk ourselves.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if settings.preorder_mode -%}
        <div class="pdp-preorder">
          <p class="pdp-preorder-head">Pre-order &middot; ships {{ settings.preorder_dispatch_label }}</p>
          <p>
            You're charged today and we email you tracking the day it ships.
            <strong>Cancel any time before dispatch for a full refund</strong> — no
            questions, no form to fill in.
          </p>
          <p class="pdp-preorder-plain">
            We're a new company making our first production run. If that date moves,
            you'll hear it from us before you hear it anywhere else.
          </p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="pdp-form">

        {%- form 'product', product -%}
          {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
            <div class="pdp-field">
              <label for="pdp-variant">Option</label>
              <select id="pdp-variant" name="id">
                {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
                  <option
                    value="{{ variant.id }}"
                    {% if variant == current_variant %}selected{% endif %}
                    {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
                  >
                    {{ variant.title }} — {{ variant.price | money }}
                    {%- unless variant.available %} (sold out){% endunless -%}
                  </option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
            </div>
          {%- else -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ current_variant.id }}">
          {%- endunless -%}

          <div class="pdp-field">
            <label for="pdp-qty">Quantity</label>
            <input id="pdp-qty" type="number" name="quantity" min="1" value="1" inputmode="numeric">
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Compatibility gate. The kit is useless without an iPhone, and the
            reels it exists to produce need Pro on top — both are disclosed in
            section 3 of the Mount Kit Terms, but nobody reads clause 3 of a
            document linked from the footer. A buyer who could not reasonably
            have known is entitled to a refund under the consumer guarantees
            whatever the terms say, so the disclosure has to sit here, at the
            point of decision.

            The checkbox is deliberately an acknowledgement rather than a
            notice: it stops the sale instead of curing it afterwards, and it
            costs a genuine buyer one second.

            It gates the dynamic checkout button as well as add-to-cart —
            "Buy it now" skips the cart entirely, so the cart-page notice would
            never be seen by those buyers.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="pdp-compat">
            <p class="pdp-compat-head">Before you buy</p>
            <p>
              <strong>Requires an iPhone running iOS {{ section.settings.min_ios }} or later.</strong>
              There is no Android app — the mount will hold an Android phone, but
              nothing will clip your shots.
            </p>
            <p>
              Recording and trimming are free. <strong>Automatic highlight reels need
              Clippar Pro</strong> ({{ section.settings.pro_price }}, free trial).
            </p>
            <p class="pdp-compat-link">
              Full detail in the <a href="/pages/mount-kit-terms-of-sale">Mount Kit Terms of Sale</a>.
            </p>
          </div>

          {%- if current_variant.available -%}
            <label class="pdp-ack" for="pdp-compat-ack">
              <input type="checkbox" id="pdp-compat-ack">
              <span>I have an iPhone running iOS {{ section.settings.min_ios }} or later.</span>
            </label>

            <button class="btn-submit pdp-add" type="submit" id="pdp-add-btn" disabled>
              {{ section.settings.add_label }}
            </button>
            <div id="pdp-dynamic-checkout" class="pdp-dynamic-disabled">
              {{ form | payment_button }}
            </div>
          {%- else -%}
            <button class="btn-submit pdp-add" type="button" disabled>Sold out</button>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endform -%}

        {%- if section.settings.note != blank -%}
          <p class="form-note">{{ section.settings.note }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
        <ul class="pdp-points">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ block.settings.text }}</li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="pdp-description">
        {{ product.description }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .pdp {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--content-grid);
    background: var(--bg);
    /* body:not(.template-index) already reserves --nav-h; clearing the fixed
       nav a second time here left a large empty band above the title. */
    padding-block: clamp(32px, 6vw, 56px) clamp(64px, 8vw, 96px);
  }

  .pdp-grid {
    grid-column: 2;
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .pdp-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .pdp-panel {
      position: sticky;
      top: 6rem;
    }
  }

  .pdp-media {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .pdp-media-item img,
  .pdp-media-item video {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg2);
  }

  .pdp-media-empty {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border: 1px dashed var(--border);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .pdp-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--green);
    margin-block-end: 0.75rem;
  }

  .pdp-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--white);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* The pre-order notice is the loudest thing in the panel after the price,
     on purpose. It answers "when do I get it" before the buyer has to ask. */
  .pdp-preorder {
    border: 1px solid var(--green);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    margin-block-end: 1.25rem;
    background: rgba(168, 230, 61, 0.08);
  }

  .pdp-preorder p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--white);
    margin: 0 0 0.55rem 0;
  }

  .pdp-preorder p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .pdp-preorder-head {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--green) !important;
  }

  .pdp-preorder-plain { color: var(--muted) !important; font-size: 0.83rem !important; }

  .pdp-compat {
    border: 1px solid var(--green);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
    background: rgba(168, 230, 61, 0.06);
  }

  .pdp-compat p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--white);
    margin: 0 0 0.55rem 0;
  }

  .pdp-compat p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .pdp-compat-head {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--green) !important;
  }

  .pdp-compat-link { font-size: 0.8rem !important; color: var(--muted) !important; }
  .pdp-compat-link a { color: var(--muted); }

  .pdp-ack {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--white);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .pdp-ack input { margin-top: 0.2rem; width: 1rem; height: 1rem; accent-color: var(--green); flex: none; }

  /* Pointer-events rather than a disabled attribute: the dynamic checkout
     button is Shopify's own markup and cannot be disabled from here. */
  .pdp-dynamic-disabled { opacity: 0.4; pointer-events: none; }

  .pdp-price {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--green);
    margin-block: 1rem 2rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .pdp-compare {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .pdp-form {
    position: relative;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
  }

  .pdp-field {
    margin-block-end: 1rem;
  }

  .pdp-field label {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-block-end: 0.4rem;
  }

  .pdp-field select,
  .pdp-field input {
    width: 100%;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }

  .pdp-field input:focus-visible,
  .pdp-field select:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--green);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }

  .pdp-add {
    width: 100%;
    margin-block-start: 0.5rem;
  }

  .pdp-add[disabled] {
    opacity: 0.45;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }

  .pdp-form .shopify-payment-button {
    margin-block-start: 0.75rem;
  }

  .pdp-points {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .pdp-points li {
    position: relative;
    padding-inline-start: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .pdp-points li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-start: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 0.45rem;
    height: 0.45rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--green);
  }

  .pdp-description {
    margin-block-start: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .pdp-description h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--white);
    margin-block: 1.75rem 0.75rem;
  }

  .pdp-description ul {
    padding-inline-start: 1.1rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .pdp-description strong {
    color: var(--white);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:general.product",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "AI-powered golf recording system"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "min_ios",
      "label": "Minimum iOS version",
      "info": "Must match the app's deployment target. Currently 15.1.",
      "default": "15.1"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "pro_price",
      "label": "Pro pricing line",
      "default": "A$14.99/month or A$99.99/year"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_compare_at",
      "label": "Show the struck-through compare-at price",
      "info": "Leave OFF until the kit has genuinely sold at the higher price for a real period. A was/now comparison on a product that has never been sold is a false saving under Australian Consumer Law, and the ACCC has pursued exactly this. Settled by Henry 24 Aug: $99 shown alone.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "add_label",
      "label": "Add to cart label",
      "default": "ADD TO CART"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "note",
      "label": "Note under buttons",
      "default": "30-day satisfaction guarantee. Requires the free Clippar app for iOS."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "point",
      "name": "Selling point",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Text",
          "default": "12-month clicker battery life"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
